am.com&_nc_gid=muLIcsvODCWTmcz6k8H9VQ&_nc_ss=79689&oh=00_AQSwPuuuwhaWRR-GE4dLfzNq50Mz_A3UqNg8XIpqtIfKxg&oe=6AE8AA55", "width": 1080, "height": 1920, "id": "12", "resolution": "1080x1920"}], "comments": [{"author": "enjoyjoey", "author_id": "143973941", "id": "18152854774554329", "text": "like a clip switch in visuals", "timestamp": 1793191171, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "ignorierseinfach", "author_id": "375365691", "id": "17951094486304453", "text": "The movement and combat made me quit out of the witcher 3. Not a single game made me so mad playing it", "timestamp": 1793112912, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "gabriplaysgames", "author_id": "2060480228", "id": "18125642347917698", "text": "I want to make a connection between this and historical fencing.\nIn movies, games etc. it usually happens that dudes with swords indeed have to charge the strike with the sword all the way back, and indeed as this video explains it feels very slow. In real practice it is in fact slow, and none of that is needed. We already stand in a position where the sword is ready to strike, either up so that a push is enough or behind and visually taunting. Not a lot of games, not even historical or even sword fighting games, do this.", "timestamp": 1793003374, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "webster_jst", "author_id": "631632128", "id": "18118079419808879", "text": "As an animator in the games industry, this was super cool to know", "timestamp": 1792998420, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "genkyu01", "author_id": "38201361271", "id": "18022979558945945", "text": "He s a cool guy when hes not forced into present mobile gacha games", "timestamp": 1792927690, "like_count": 1}, {"author": "raven.lionfox", "author_id": "74642929228", "id": "17990942355108391", "text": "Bro is teaching us game design for free. Let's take a brief moment to appreciate. \ud83c\udf82", "timestamp": 1792907852, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "hamza_art", "author_id": "2142602425", "id": "17864914602691983", "text": "Elden ring boss have 8/10th anticipation\ud83d\ude02", "timestamp": 1792855987, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "saulgood236", "author_id": "54446182975", "id": "17897967579655363", "text": "What about charge up attacks", "timestamp": 1792823347, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "moobeef2", "author_id": "1424607395", "id": "18098581826544803", "text": "You explained this so well and thanks for sharing!", "timestamp": 1792769207, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "jase_3d_artist", "author_id": "7456913216", "id": "17908476801333554", "text": "Exactly. \ud83d\udc4f\ud83d\udd25", "timestamp": 1792762938, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "mfahmial", "author_id": "2023015671", "id": "18092158127692363", "text": "Mhw: nah", "timestamp": 1792753210, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "soxger.x", "author_id": "1504702920", "id": "18120487456974631", "text": "Esto gratis? sube un curso viejo sabroso", "timestamp": 1792694888, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "sc_concept_artist", "author_id": "241094640", "id": "18168151612415249", "text": "I guess you could also add in a button hold for the anticipation/wind up and release of the button triggers a stronger attack and a single button press for an instant no anticipation/wind up attack which is quicker but with less power", "timestamp": 1792672565, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "ediudodesign", "author_id": "460250330", "id": "18139564129712134", "text": "Very good food for thought, thank you! \ud83d\ude01\u2764\ufe0f", "timestamp": 1792654537, "like_count": 0}], "webpage_url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DeuiO0UjRLM/", "original_url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DeuiO0UjRLM/", "webpage_url_basename": "DeuiO0UjRLM", "webpage_url_domain": "instagram.com", "extractor": "Instagram", "extractor_key": "Instagram", "playlist": null, "playlist_index": null, "thumbnail": "https://scontent-sjc3-1.cdninstagram.com/v/t51.82787-15/858180132_18628679515045434_1624808089844700752_n.jpg?stp=dst-jpg_e15_tt6&_nc_cat=110&ig_cache_key=NDAxMjI5NDg2OTg2NzEwNzAyMDE4NjI4Njc5NTEy